1 NOTE Gil Aires Moniz was a secretary to the famous constable, Pereira in the rein of Joao I.
2 CONT Gil Aires Moniz founded the temple of the Piedad in the Carmelite Monastary at Lisbon. The Moniz family had the right of interment for all time and it so happened that the body of Philipa Moniz, Columbus' wife, duly rested. Her so
2 CONC n, Diogo, (Diego Columbus), later ordered her mortal remains moved and reburied in the church of Santa Clara in Santo Domingo. She had another daughter, Violante Moniz who had married, Mulier or Muliartes in Huelva and their son, 
2 CONC Bartolomo was heir to governorship of Porto Santo.
2 CONT He was still a boy so she ceded governorship to Pedro Correa Cunha who later married, Iseult, the daughter of Bartolomo by his first wife.
2 CONT Source:
2 CONT Historia Genealogica de Casa Real Portuguesa,
2 CONT D. Antonio Caetano de Sousa,
2 CONT Atlantida Livaria editora, Lda, 2a Edizao Coimbra, 1946
