1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The Ducal Palace of Vila Viçosa (Portuguese: Paço Ducal de Vila Viçosa) is a royal palace in Portugal, located in the civil parish of Nossa Senhora da Conceição, in the municipality of Vila Viçosa, in the Alentejo,
2 CONC  situated about 150 km (93 miles) east of the capital Lisbon. It was for many centuries the seat of the House of Braganza, one of the most important noble houses in Portugal. Braganza was the ruling house of the Kingdom of Portuga
2 CONC l from 1640 until 1910, when King Manuel II, titular head of the family, was deposed in the 5 October 1910 Revolution which brought in a Republican government
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ducal_Palace_of_Vila_Vi%C3%A7osa#:~:text=The%20Ducal%20Palace%20of%20Vila,brought%20in%20a%20Republican%20government.
