1 NOTE 	1  NAME Bartholomew /Perestrello/
2 CONT 	2  SOUR S43
2 CONT 	3  PAGE p. 13
2 CONT 	1  NAME Bartolomeu /Perestrelo/
2 CONT 	2  SOUR S3
2 CONT 	3  PAGE p. 104
1 NOTE Bartolomo Perestrello and his brother, Rafael were members of the Counsel at the city of Lisbon.
2 CONT In 1442 after Infante Joao died, Bartolomo was designated as a cavallero, knight. He signed a Real Cedula as a representaive de la cuidad de Braganza accepting Infante pedro as a regent of the household of the Infante Enrique, "Th
2 CONC e Navigator;" under whose authority he went to colonize the Island de Porto Santo. Fernando Columbo in his bigraphy wrote that Bartolomo discovered Porto santo in the year of 1418. A contradiction arose when the historian, Zurata 
2 CONC wrote that Bartolomo went to that island when it was being settled in the year of 1430.  In the year of 1446 Bartolomo was granted a real cedula proclaiming him as hereditary governor of Porto Santo. In that same document Enrique 
2 CONC proclaims that Bartolomo is a gentleman of the Infante's house.
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT Agostinho de Ornellas, Memoria Sobre Descubrimiento America, Typographia Academia Real de Sciencias 1882.
2 CONT Freitas, pp 29-34.
2 CONT Documentos Archivo Historico Camara Municipal de Lisbon, Officinas Graficas Casa de Moeda de Lisbon 1959.
2 CONT Marie Montiero Velho Arrudo, Documentos Descubrimiento e Provamiento dos Acores, Porta Delgado, Portugal 1932, pp 107-117.
2 CONT Perragallo, pp 19-27, 45-51.
2 CONT Silva Vol 1, P 244,
