2 DATE 17 NOV 1525
1 OCCU Maid of the Queen regnant of Castile, Joanna La Beltraneja.
1 TITL II
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ana de Mendonça (1460-1542) was a maid of the Queen regnant of Castile, Joanna la Beltraneja, and a mistress of King John II of Portugal, who was also Master of the Order of Saint James 1470-1492. They had one son,
2 CONC  Jorge de Lancastre, Duke of Coimbra and Master of the Military Order of Saint James of the Sword.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ana de Mendonça's father was a knight of Saint James named Nuno Furtado de Mendonça, (Bartolomeu Perestrelo's brother-in-law) married to Leonor da Silva, a descendant of King Afonso III of Portugal. Ana de Mendonça's grandfather w
2 CONC as Afonso Furtado de Mendonça "anadél-mor de Besteiros" (leader of the archers,) a post that was then inherited by Ana de Mendonça's uncle, Duarte Furtado de Mendonça.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Ana de Mendonça, niece of Bartolomeu Perestrelo, took over the post of "Comendadeira" (Mother Superior) in the All Saints Monastery belonging to the Order of Saint James of the Sword on July 8, 1508, a position she held until her 
2 CONC death in 1542.[2] The previous Comendadeira had been her aunt, Violante Nogueira, Bartolomeu Perestrelo's sister-in-law, the former nanny of King Duarte's children, and aunt of Izeu Perestrelo, Filipa Moniz's half-sister. Ana de M
2 CONC endonça was direct cousin of Izeu Perestrelo (Captainess of Graciosa Island) married to King John II's Royal Guard, Pedro Correia da Cunha Captain of Graciosa Island.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1  Manuel Abranches de Soveral, «Os Furtado de Mendonça portugueses. Ensaio sobre a sua verdadeira origem», Porto 2004 2 Prof. Joel Mata, A Comunidade Feminina da Ordem de Santiago: A comenda de Santos na Idade Média. Universidade
2 CONC  do Porto, 1992 3  Prof. Luis Adão da Fonseca, D. João II, Temas e Debates, 2007.
2 CONT
2 CONT in, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ana_de_Mendon%C3%A7a
